From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 09:00:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(block-entities): translate moving and extended pistons

Bedrock stores piston extension in the PistonArm block entity and the carried block in a separate MovingBlock entity. Translate both into Java block states and moving-piston data so the client can render the animation and its carried block. The mapping follows fields captured from a native 1.26.51 server and uses the existing block-state sanitizer for carried blocks.

Geyser sends MovingBlock tags before the new PistonArm progress and does not supply a moving head entity. Ignore stale opposite-direction progress, synthesize the arm animation, and refresh carried tags across chunk boundaries. Java 26.3 creates moving piston entities only from local piston events, so the addon must create them for translated block updates. Tests cover native progress reversal, stale tags and head/base animation positions. Evidence: GeyserMC/Geyser core translator/level/block/entity/PistonBlockEntity.java and Java 26.3 MovingPistonBlock/ClientPacketListener bytecode.
